[ Prompts ]  ← Instructions
                         ↓
                   [ LLM ]     ← Brain (reasoning, language generation)
                                                                  ↓
                                                              [ Agent Framework ]  ← Orchestration (memory, tools, APIs)
                                                                                                                 ↓
                                                                                                       [ Agent ]   ← Real-world assistant (DevOps bot, Finance bot, etc.)


Summary :

LLM = brain (reasoning & text generation)

Prompting = language you use to “program” the brain

Agent Framework = structure that gives the LLM memory, tools, decision loops

Agent = packaged solution (LLM + prompts + tools) for a specific use case

So the Hierarchy is:
Prompts → LLM → Agent Framework → Agent (real-world use case)
